# Explain the why

This repo is an interview-prep sandbox (trade support / exchange operations, London). The owner wants to learn from
it and be able to explain it. When adding or editing code, SQL, docs or exercises:

- Add short comments that say **why** a choice was made (design trade-off, real-world cause, what breaks otherwise),
  not only what the code does.
- For any new exercise or anomaly, include a `WHY:` line (why it matters in production) and, in the solutions file,
  the expected result and the reasoning.
- Verify factual claims (regulation, dates, FIX version behaviour) against a source before writing them; note the
  check date for anything that changes over time.
- Keep the project simple: standard library, SQLite, flat files. No frameworks or web UI.
- Do not print or hard-code the five anomaly order IDs outside `solutions/` and the `--answer-key` flag.
- After changing `db/seed_db.py`, run it and confirm the self-check prints `Done - 0 errors.`
